From: pocket_vm developers <pocket-vm@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] um: define PTRACE_SYSEMU for headers that omit it

This header already supplies PTRACE_SYSEMU_SINGLESTEP for glibc before
2.27.  Those same versions also leave out PTRACE_SYSEMU itself, which
userspace_tramp()'s ptrace path uses, so define it the same way.
---
 arch/x86/um/shared/sysdep/ptrace_user.h | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/x86/um/shared/sysdep/ptrace_user.h b/arch/x86/um/shared/sysdep/ptrace_user.h
index 98da231..fc0e5d0 100644
--- a/arch/x86/um/shared/sysdep/ptrace_user.h
+++ b/arch/x86/um/shared/sysdep/ptrace_user.h
@@ -18,3 +18,8 @@
 #ifndef PTRACE_SYSEMU_SINGLESTEP
 #define PTRACE_SYSEMU_SINGLESTEP 32
 #endif
+
+/* Likewise PTRACE_SYSEMU itself, which those versions also leave out. */
+#ifndef PTRACE_SYSEMU
+#define PTRACE_SYSEMU 31
+#endif
